            "C": "The monitoring failure was in the second line of defense — risk management should have identified rule #37's vulnerability during the system's initial implementation rather than relying on internal audit to detect it.",
            "D": "Annual monitoring is inadequate when risk velocity is high because $1.7M in fraud loss accumulated in just 11 months. COSO Principle 16 requires that monitoring frequency be calibrated to the speed at which risk can materialize and cause damage — for high-volume, high-dollar transaction systems, continuous monitoring or exception-based analytics are the appropriate benchmark, not annual point-in-time testing."
