        "Stem": "Paxford Consumer Products, a $2.4B manufacturer of household goods, acquires LuxeClean, a $180M premium cleaning products brand, to enter the fast-growing premium segment. During due diligence, the acquisition team — led by CFO Robert Chen — identified LuxeClean's inventory costing methodology as non-standard but reconcilable and proceeded with the transaction. Post-acquisition, Paxford's controller discovers that LuxeClean had been capitalizing routine maintenance costs as fixed asset improvements for four years, overstating net income by an average of $3.2M annually. The acquisition was priced at 14x reported EBITDA, resulting in an estimated $44.8M of overpayment relative to true earnings. Which best evaluates whether the risk assessment during strategy-setting adequately considered financial reporting risk?",
