        "Stem": "Alderway Corporation restated its financial statements after discovering that revenue had been overstated by 18% over two fiscal years due to premature recognition of bill-and-hold transactions. Following the restatement, the board exercised a clawback provision in the CEO's employment agreement and recovered $2.4 million in performance-based bonuses tied to the misstated results. The board issued a press release stating that 'accountability starts at the top' and that the clawback demonstrates Alderway's commitment to integrity. The audit committee has now asked the board to assess whether this action adequately addresses the tone-at-the-top requirements of COSO Principle 1. Which of the following represents the most appropriate evaluation?",
