        "ExplanationWrongB": "",
        "ExplanationWrongC": "Option C prescribes an operationally infeasible response. COSO Principle 10 does not require that all vendor payments be suspended when a control fails — it requires that compensating controls reduce the residual risk to an acceptable level. Payment suspension for six months would breach vendor contracts, disrupt supply chains, and likely cause more business harm than the control gap. COSO expects organizations to design compensating controls that allow operations to continue while maintaining acceptable control coverage — not to halt operations entirely.",
